Why Do Period Cramps Happen? Understanding Menstrual Cramps

Period cramps are one of the most common symptoms people experience during menstruation. For some, cramps are mild and manageable, while others experience stronger discomfort that can affect their daily routine.

Understanding why menstrual cramps happen can help you recognise common symptoms and know when it may be appropriate to seek medical advice.

What Causes Period Cramps?

The uterus is a muscular organ that prepares itself for a possible pregnancy during the menstrual cycle.

When pregnancy does not occur, the uterine lining is shed during menstruation. The uterus contracts to help remove this lining.

These contractions are influenced by chemicals called prostaglandins. Higher prostaglandin activity can cause stronger uterine contractions, which may result in more noticeable cramps.

What Do Menstrual Cramps Feel Like?

Period cramps are usually felt in the lower abdomen. Some people may also experience discomfort in the lower back or thighs.

Other symptoms can include:

Nausea
Headache
Tiredness
Bloating
Loose stools
General discomfort

Symptoms can vary from one person to another.

How Can You Manage Mild Cramps?

Heat is a commonly used method for menstrual discomfort. A warm heating pad or hot-water bottle placed over the lower abdomen may help relax the muscles.

Gentle movement can also be helpful for some people. Walking, stretching, or light yoga may make you feel more comfortable.

Adequate rest and sleep are also important. If exercise makes your symptoms worse, there is no need to push yourself.

Staying hydrated and eating balanced meals can support your general wellbeing during your period.

Can the Right Period Product Improve Comfort?

While a sanitary pad does not treat menstrual cramps, the right menstrual product can make your period experience more comfortable.

A pad that moves, leaks, or feels uncomfortable can add unnecessary stress when you are already dealing with cramps.

Choosing the correct size and absorbency for your flow can help you feel more secure.

